#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:4
msgid "Backing up the sources of third-party dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:6
msgid ""
"The :ref:`sources backup feature<conan_backup_sources>` transparently "
"uploads the sources downloaded by recipes (from Github releases, project web "
"pages, etc.) to a server of your own, so that future builds are reproducible "
"even if the original URLs disappear. By default, those backups are uploaded "
"together with the packages with :command:`conan upload`. But what if we want "
"to back up the sources of our dependencies **without** building and "
"uploading any package? This is the case for example for populating the "
"backup server from a CI job, or for dependencies that are already available "
"in a remote as binaries, and that would be skipped during the upload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:13
msgid ""
"There are two ways to do that, both ending with the :ref:`conan cache backup-"
"upload<reference_commands_cache>` command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:15
msgid ""
"Retrieving the sources of a full dependency graph with :command:`conan graph "
"info` and ``tools.build:download_source=True``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:16
msgid "Retrieving the sources of a single recipe with :command:`conan source`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:18
msgid ""
"The ``backup-upload`` command uploads **all** the source backups that are in "
"the cache, regardless of which package they belong to, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:23
msgid "Configuring the backup server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:25
msgid ""
"Let's define the "
"following :ref:`global.conf<reference_config_files_global_conf>`, using the "
"URL of a backup repository that accepts ``PUT`` and ``GET`` HTTP methods "
"(see :ref:`how to create one in "
"Artifactory<devops_artifactory_backup_sources_repo>`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:29
msgid "global.conf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:29
msgid ""
"core.sources:upload_url=https://myteam.myorg.com/artifactory/backup-"
"sources/\n"
"core.sources:download_urls=[\"origin\", \"https://myteam.myorg.com/"
"artifactory/backup-sources/\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:35
msgid ""
"If the repository requires authentication, define it in "
"the :ref:`source_credentials.json<reference_config_files_source_credentials>` "
"file. Check the :ref:`sources backup configuration<backup_sources_config>` "
"for the rest of the available configuration items, like "
"``core.sources:exclude_urls``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:41
msgid "Backing up the sources of a dependency graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:43
msgid ""
"Recipes download their sources in the ``source()`` method, that is only "
"executed when the package is built from source. The "
"``tools.build:download_source=True`` conf forces the execution of "
"``source()`` for all the packages in the graph, even if there are binaries "
"available, without needing to build anything. This can be done "
"with :command:`conan graph info` (or :command:`conan install`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:48
msgid ""
"$ conan graph info --requires=libiconv/1.17 -c "
"tools.build:download_source=True"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:53
msgid ""
"Recall that the ``conan graph info`` can also work with a "
"``conanfile.txt/.py`` instead of a ``--requires`` argument. Once the sources "
"are downloaded to the Conan cache (to the ``core.sources:download_cache`` "
"folder), we can upload all of them to the backup server:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:57
msgid ""
"$ conan cache backup-upload\n"
"\n"
"-------- Uploading backup sources --------\n"
"Uploading summary "
"'8f74213b56238c85a50a5329f77e06198771e70dd9a739779f4c02f65d971313.json' to "
"backup sources server\n"
"Uploading file "
"'8f74213b56238c85a50a5329f77e06198771e70dd9a739779f4c02f65d971313' to backup "
"sources server\n"
"Upload backup sources complete"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:66
msgid ""
"Each source is stored in the backup server with the ``sha256`` of the "
"downloaded file as name, plus a ``.json`` file with the references and "
"original URLs that the file belongs to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:69
msgid "8f74213b56238c85a50a5329f77e06198771e70dd9a739779f4c02f65d971313.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:69
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"references\": {\n"
"    \"libiconv/1.17\": [\n"
"      \"https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/gnu/libiconv/libiconv-1.17.tar.gz\",\n"
"      \"https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/libiconv/libiconv-1.17.tar.gz\"\n"
"    ]\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"timestamp\": 1794226585\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:84
msgid ""
"Only the sources downloaded with ``get()`` or ``download()`` providing a "
"``sha256`` are backed up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:85
msgid ""
"The ``tools.build:download_source=True`` conf applies to all the packages in "
"the graph, including the ``tool_requires``, so their sources will be backed "
"up too. It can be restricted to some packages with the conf pattern syntax, "
"like ``-c libiconv/*:tools.build:download_source=True``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:88
msgid ""
"Sources that were fetched from a URL in ``core.sources:exclude_urls`` are "
"not uploaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:92
msgid ""
"The ``source()`` method is not executed for the packages whose binaries are "
"skipped from the graph, as they are not necessary in the current "
"configuration (for example the dependencies of a shared library that are not "
"needed by its consumers). The sources of those packages will not be "
"downloaded, so they will not be backed up either. To make sure that the "
"sources of **all** the packages in the graph are retrieved, disable the "
"binaries skip with the ``tools.graph:skip_binaries=False`` conf:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:98
msgid ""
"# This will only work for packages in the \"host\" context, not build tools\n"
"# Use \"-c:a\" if you want to download the sources for \"tool-requires\" "
"too\n"
"$ conan graph info --requires=libiconv/1.17 -c "
"tools.build:download_source=True -c tools.graph:skip_binaries=False"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:106
msgid "Backing up the sources of a single recipe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:108
msgid ""
"If we have the recipe in a folder, for example in the Conan Center Index "
"repository or in our own recipes repository, we can run the :command:`conan "
"source` command directly, which only executes the ``source()`` method "
"without building anything:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:112
msgid "conanfile.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:112
msgid ""
"from conan import ConanFile\n"
"from conan.tools.files import get\n"
"\n"
"class ZlibRecipe(ConanFile):\n"
"    name = \"zlib\"\n"
"    version = \"1.3.1\"\n"
"\n"
"    def source(self):\n"
"        get(self, **self.conan_data[\"sources\"][self.version], "
"strip_root=True)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:125
msgid "conandata.yml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:125
msgid ""
"sources:\n"
"  \"1.3.1\":\n"
"    url: \"https://github.com/madler/zlib/releases/download/v1.3.1/"
"zlib-1.3.1.tar.gz\"\n"
"    sha256: "
"\"9a93b2b7dfdac77ceba5a558a580e74667dd6fede4585b91eefb60f03b72df23\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:133
msgid ""
"$ conan source .\n"
"Getting sources for conanfile.py (zlib/1.3.1)\n"
"Calling source() in /home/user/zlib\n"
"Sources correctly downloaded from https://github.com/madler/zlib/releases/"
"download/v1.3.1/zlib-1.3.1.tar.gz\n"
"Uncompressing zlib-1.3.1.tar.gz to .\n"
"\n"
"$ conan cache backup-upload\n"
"-------- Uploading backup sources --------\n"
"Uploading summary "
"'9a93b2b7dfdac77ceba5a558a580e74667dd6fede4585b91eefb60f03b72df23.json' to "
"backup sources server\n"
"Uploading file "
"'9a93b2b7dfdac77ceba5a558a580e74667dd6fede4585b91eefb60f03b72df23' to backup "
"sources server\n"
"Upload backup sources complete"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:147
msgid ""
"This approach can be automated for many recipes by simply looping over their "
"folders, and then uploading all the backups at once with a single ``conan "
"cache backup-upload``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:152
msgid "Using the backup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/commands/backup_sources.rst:154
msgid ""
"Once the sources are in the backup server, any build that has the "
"``core.sources:download_urls`` conf above will be able to fetch the sources "
"from it when the original URL is not available (or before trying it, if the "
"backup server is listed first in ``core.sources:download_urls``). "
"See :ref:`how to run Conan with the backup configured<conan_backup_sources>` "
"for more details."
msgstr ""
